+//
+// Fix 146d: a hard bound. A newer picture is never held once the one on screen has been there two
+// periods (the limit's own most is one period; this guards any count that went wrong). On the
+// console with the 146b limit, single pictures stayed 162-681 ms while the game's own longest
+// gap was 31-43 ms, also with the limit not applied. The presents missing in those windows
+// (0.5-2.7 a second of 120) match those times, so the presents themselves stopped (the UI thread
+// or the display), which no gate can show through. The summary now gives the longest present
+// interval and how many were over 100 ms, so the next log tells the two apart.
